worktree: ../okay-wt-adaptive
spec: specs/resilience.md — the one box left open, deliberately

why: the box has been deferred twice with a reason, and the reason is
  now "no measurement", not "no machinery". A gradient controller
  tuned against no traffic is a guess with extra steps, so this lane
  builds the MEASUREMENT first and lets it decide.

what: a deterministic harness — virtual clock, a downstream whose
  latency rises with in-flight count and whose CAPACITY HALVES
  mid-run (the case a fixed permit count cannot follow, and the only
  case where an adaptive one earns anything). Compare a fixed
  Bulkhead at several permit counts against a gradient one on
  throughput, tail latency and rejections. No wall clock, so the
  numbers do not move with the box.

  The gate: adaptive lands ONLY if it beats the best fixed setting on
  the changing-capacity workload and does not lose badly on the
  steady one. If it does not, the refutation lands instead — with its
  numbers, in the spec, so nobody builds it again.

next: harness, numbers, then either the controller or the refutation
